(7676049, 1254334, 100393, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by photoboy19:</b></div><hr/><i> a bit heavy on the grain for me </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Appreciate that. Nothing added from me though - this is how it came out of the camera, albeit with the camera''s ''grainy black and white'' filter applied, in conjunction with the pinhole.</td>', 'Originally posted by photoboy19: a bit heavy on the grain for me   Appreciate that. Nothing added from me though - this is how it came out of the camera, albeit with the camera''s ''grainy black and white'' filter applied, in conjunction with the pinhole.', '2020-10-07 06:50:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7676050, 1254738, 259105, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Great photo and congrats on 4th place, you just missed out on a ribbon. What I really liked about the photo is a) the composition and b) the story that the photo tells and I think you did a great job. I love the fog and the wetness and the terrible weather in this photo because it really does show that he''ll work in any weather. <br/> <br/>Technical: The composition is great. The bit of blur on the mans shovel shows that he''s moving and doing his work instead of just posing for you. The amount of detail in the water is incredible.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to PM me!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Great photo and congrats on 4th place, you just missed out on a ribbon. What I really liked about the photo is a) the composition and b) the story that the photo tells and I think you did a great job. I love the fog and the wetness and the terrible weather in this photo because it really does show that he''ll work in any weather.  Technical: The composition is great. The bit of blur on the mans shovel shows that he''s moving and doing his work instead of just posing for you. The amount of detail in the water is incredible. If you have any questions feel free to PM me!', '2020-10-07 08:54:33.000000', NULL, 0),
